  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Waaagh!" id="6ac2-fce9-ef59-43eb" hidden="false">
      <description>You can re-roll the Advance roll.
While the unit is riled up, the unit has a 5+ invulnerable save.
While the unit is riled up, ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit gain [ASSAULT].
-&gt; When the unit is selected to make an Advance move: while the unit is riled up, the triggering unit is eligible to declare a charge even if it Advanced this turn.
-&gt; At the start of the Command phase, you may use this ability, once per battle per army, until the end of the next turn: all friendly ORKS units with the Waaagh ability are riled up.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Da Boss" id="6415-b617-d268-762c" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle round, while this model has the Da Boss ability, while this model is the Warlord, you gain 1CP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unstable energies" id="ef60-7b2a-ef20-bea6" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle round, all friendly ORKS PSYKER units' psychic level becomes their Psyker Level characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Move Types" id="e605-279f-ae10-621c" hidden="false">
      <description>Pulse Jet move:
  - The unit can move up to D6+18".
  - While it moves, the unit can move over terrain features and models as though they were not there; the unit ignores vertical distances when it moves; the unit cannot end a move within Engagement Range of any enemy unit.
  - After it moves, until the end of the turn: the unit cannot declare a charge; until the end of the turn: the unit cannot start an Action; until the start of your next turn: the attacking unit gets -1 to Hit rolls.
Assault Disembark move (the Assault mode of a Disembark move):
  - Each model is set up wholly within 3" of that Transport.
  - A unit can make this move only if the unit is embarked and the Transport this unit is embarked within is on the battlefield and the unit did not embark this phase and not (the Transport this unit is embarked within advanced this phase or the Transport this unit is embarked within fell back this phase).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
